drm/amd/display: opt-in DSC decoder advertisement for PCONs that hide it

Experimental, off by default: amdgpu.bc250_pcon_force_dsc=1.

Some DP-to-HDMI 2.1 converters whose silicon carries a DSC 1.2a decoder
ship firmware that advertises neither DSC nor FEC to the source. A Cable
Matters 102101 (Synaptics VMM7100, firmware 7.02.120) reads all zeros
from DP_DSC_SUPPORT through DP_DSC_BITS_PER_PIXEL_INC and 0 at
DP_FEC_CAPABILITY on this board. DC believes it, the DP 1.4 link cannot
carry 4K120 RGB uncompressed, and the stream falls back to YCbCr 4:2:2
10-bit -- while the same TV on a CH7218 PCON gets RGB 12-bit with DSC.

With the parameter set, a DP-to-HDMI converter whose DSC capability
block is entirely zero is treated as a DSC 1.2a decoder with FEC, using
the block a known-good CH7218 reports as the template (DSC 1.2, 12 bpp
max, RGB/4:4:4/4:2:2, 8/10/12 bpc, 2560 px slices, DSC_SUPPORT set,
passthrough clear). The source then encodes DSC and writes DSC enable
to the PCON as it would for any decoder. Adapters that advertise any DSC
capability at all are left exactly as reported, so this cannot touch a
CH7218 or any correctly-described unit.

This is a probe of the adapter's firmware, not a fix: if the firmware
really cannot decode, every mode that needs DSC comes up black or
corrupted, and the parameter has to go. It logs at warning level what it
overrode so the state is visible in a plain dmesg.

Plumbing mirrors bc250_ch7218_quirk: module parameter -> dc_config
flag -> one gated helper called right after the CH7218 DSC restore in
retrieve_link_cap(), where dongle_type is already known.

---

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu.h b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu.h
index a44390d..7ec3301 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu.h
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu.h
@@ -257,6 +257,7 @@ extern int amdgpu_vcnfw_log;
 extern int amdgpu_sg_display;
 extern int amdgpu_bc250_hdmi21;
 extern int amdgpu_bc250_ch7218_quirk;
+extern int amdgpu_bc250_pcon_force_dsc;
 extern int amdgpu_umsch_mm;
 extern int amdgpu_seamless;
 extern int amdgpu_umsch_mm_fwlog;
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_drv.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_drv.c
index 4320891..14f9123 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_drv.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_drv.c
@@ -237,6 +237,7 @@ int amdgpu_vcnfw_log;
 int amdgpu_sg_display = -1; /* auto */
 int amdgpu_bc250_hdmi21 = 1;
 int amdgpu_bc250_ch7218_quirk;
+int amdgpu_bc250_pcon_force_dsc;
 int amdgpu_user_partt_mode = AMDGPU_AUTO_COMPUTE_PARTITION_MODE;
 int amdgpu_umsch_mm;
 int amdgpu_seamless = -1; /* auto */
@@ -1007,6 +1008,25 @@ module_param_named(bc250_hdmi21, amdgpu_bc250_hdmi21, int, 0444);
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(bc250_ch7218_quirk, "BC-250: opt-in CH7218 DP-to-HDMI 2.1 adapter quirk (0 = disabled (default), 1 = enabled)");
 module_param_named(bc250_ch7218_quirk, amdgpu_bc250_ch7218_quirk, int, 0444);
 
+/**
+ * DOC: bc250_pcon_force_dsc (int)
+ * BC-250 (Cyan Skillfish, DCN 2.0.1) only. Experimental, opt-in. Some DP to
+ * HDMI 2.1 converters whose silicon has a DSC 1.2a decoder ship firmware that
+ * advertises neither DSC nor FEC in the DPCD (a Cable Matters 102101 on a
+ * Synaptics VMM7100 with firmware 7.02.120 reads all zeros). Without DSC the
+ * DP 1.4 link cannot carry 4K120 RGB and the driver falls back to YCbCr
+ * 4:2:2. With this set, a DP-to-HDMI converter that reports an all-zero DSC
+ * capability block is treated as a DSC 1.2a decoder with FEC, using the
+ * capability block a known-good CH7218 PCON reports, so the source encodes
+ * DSC and asks the adapter to decode it. If the adapter's firmware really
+ * cannot, modes that need DSC come up black or corrupted: remove the
+ * parameter. Adapters that advertise any DSC capability are left alone.
+ * Requires bc250_hdmi21=1 (the default).
+ * (0 = disabled (default), 1 = enabled)
+ */
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(bc250_pcon_force_dsc, "BC-250: experimental, advertise a DSC 1.2a decoder and FEC on behalf of a DP-to-HDMI 2.1 adapter that reports none (0 = disabled (default), 1 = enabled)");
+module_param_named(bc250_pcon_force_dsc, amdgpu_bc250_pcon_force_dsc, int, 0444);
+
 /**
  * DOC: umsch_mm (int)
  * Enable Multi Media User Mode Scheduler. This is a HW scheduling engine for VCN and VPE.
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm.c
index f9861b5..8906549 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm.c
@@ -963,6 +963,7 @@ static int amdgpu_dm_init(struct amdgpu_device *adev)
 
 	init_data.flags.bc250_hdmi21 = (amdgpu_bc250_hdmi21 != 0);
 	init_data.flags.bc250_ch7218_quirk = (amdgpu_bc250_ch7218_quirk != 0);
+	init_data.flags.bc250_pcon_force_dsc = (amdgpu_bc250_pcon_force_dsc != 0);
 
 	init_data.flags.seamless_boot_edp_requested = false;
 
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/dc/dc.h b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/dc/dc.h
index b0c8426..6df6bcf 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/dc/dc.h
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/dc/dc.h
@@ -604,6 +604,7 @@ struct dc_config {
 	bool enable_frl;
